WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.730
A Aoyama Rei 

00:00:01.270 --> 00:00:02.730
Is Komaba here?

00:00:03.190 --> 00:00:04.980
He's not back yet.

00:00:04.980 --> 00:00:05.860
Still?

00:00:05.860 --> 00:00:08.560
He's been gone for a whole week.

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:10.600
Is he down with a cold?

00:00:10.600 --> 00:00:13.250
Dunno. I haven't heard anything.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:15.870
This is a handout from practicum.

00:00:15.870 --> 00:00:17.920
Can you give it to him 
when he gets back?

00:00:17.920 --> 00:00:18.580
Sure.

00:00:19.140 --> 00:00:23.260
Nakajima-sensei's also been out
 sick for a while now.

00:00:23.260 --> 00:00:25.530
Maybe a cold's going around.

00:00:28.380 --> 00:00:30.590
<b>Cheese Processing Room</b>

00:02:08.540 --> 00:02:13.500
<b>Fall Chapter Episode 8
Hachiken 
 Howls</b>

00:02:16.070 --> 00:02:18.030
Oh, Nakajima-sensei!

00:02:18.030 --> 00:02:20.120
Good morning.

00:02:20.120 --> 00:02:22.010
Are you feeling better?

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.010
We've been worried about you!

00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:26.750
We are going to make cheese.

00:02:28.370 --> 00:02:31.870
Grief for cheese can 
only be assuaged by more cheese.

00:02:31.870 --> 00:02:34.460
What did you all eat 
yesterday and today?

00:02:34.460 --> 00:02:36.150
You mean the menu?

00:02:36.150 --> 00:02:38.160
Yesterday, the dorm breakfast...

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:41.900
was rice, miso soup, 
braised fish, pickles...

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.590
Lunch was fried cutlet bento,

00:02:43.590 --> 00:02:44.700
and dinner was udon.

00:02:44.700 --> 00:02:46.700
We haven't eaten 
breakfast yet today,

00:02:46.700 --> 00:02:48.780
but I think the menu said 
an omelette and salad.

00:02:48.780 --> 00:02:51.590
Hm, what'd I eat?

00:02:52.150 --> 00:02:57.340
Before I came to school, I had rice,
 miso soup, natto, eggs...

00:02:57.340 --> 00:02:59.220
Kino-kun, you're not needed.

00:02:59.220 --> 00:03:01.450
Mikage-san, Hachiken-kun, 
come with me.

00:03:01.450 --> 00:03:03.570
What? Why—

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:04.620
Ow!

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:05.830
Don't touch me!

00:03:06.340 --> 00:03:07.440
Corporal punishment!

00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:08.610
It's just the back of the hand!

00:03:08.610 --> 00:03:11.400
Kino-kun, you will take care 
of the horses by yourself.

00:03:11.400 --> 00:03:12.800
What was that for?

00:03:12.800 --> 00:03:13.290
So mean!

00:03:13.610 --> 00:03:17.740
<i>I, Nakajima, will become 
a demon for cheese!</i>

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:21.260
Wow, so warm!

00:03:21.260 --> 00:03:23.760
The temperature here is 
maintained at 30 degrees Celsius.

00:03:24.060 --> 00:03:25.330
What's this?

00:03:25.330 --> 00:03:27.060
A giant egg slicer?

00:03:30.200 --> 00:03:32.490
What do you want, Tokiwa?

00:03:32.490 --> 00:03:34.990
I passed by while walking Vice Prez

00:03:34.990 --> 00:03:37.860
and smelled something tasty cookin'!

00:03:37.860 --> 00:03:39.470
And you, Yoshino-san?

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:43.240
My woman's instincts told me to go
 to the cheese processing room!

00:03:43.780 --> 00:03:47.880
You both live in the dorms, so you ate 
the same food as these two, right?

00:03:49.340 --> 00:03:50.320
Very well.

00:03:50.320 --> 00:03:52.310
Come in and help.

00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:53.960
Yay!

00:03:54.680 --> 00:03:57.170
Today, we'll make a type 
of cheese called raclette.

00:03:57.580 --> 00:04:00.340
We'll use 120 liters of milk.

00:04:00.340 --> 00:04:02.380
That's like a milk bath!

00:04:02.380 --> 00:04:03.850
First, we pasteurize.

00:04:04.390 --> 00:04:08.090
We'll raise the milk temperature to 
63 degrees Celsius over 20 minutes.

00:04:08.870 --> 00:04:12.290
Please wash the tools 
in the meantime.

00:04:12.290 --> 00:04:13.140
Okay!

00:04:15.280 --> 00:04:18.570
I'm adding calcium chloride, 
Brevibacterium linens, and the starter culture.

00:04:18.910 --> 00:04:21.530
Please wash the tools 
in the meantime.

00:04:21.760 --> 00:04:22.520
Okay!

00:04:25.320 --> 00:04:28.310
We'll add rennet and 
other coagulating agents.

00:04:28.900 --> 00:04:31.500
Please wash the tools 
in the meantime.

00:04:32.260 --> 00:04:35.420
I feel like cleaning's all 
that we've been doing.

00:04:35.420 --> 00:04:40.250
Were we just brought 
here to be dishwashers?

00:04:40.780 --> 00:04:44.100
Once it thickens to a custard-like 
consistency, you can cut it.

00:04:44.100 --> 00:04:46.170
The liquid that comes out is whey.

00:04:46.170 --> 00:04:47.090
Whoa!

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:53.450
It's the stuff you can feed pigs 
to make them taste good, right?

00:04:53.450 --> 00:04:55.270
Okay, wash these, too.

00:04:55.270 --> 00:04:56.810
Okay, okay.

00:04:56.810 --> 00:04:59.400
Dang, so we're only here to clean.

00:04:59.400 --> 00:05:01.070
So boring.

00:05:01.410 --> 00:05:04.310
Want to snack on cheese curds?

00:05:04.310 --> 00:05:05.910
Yay!

00:05:05.910 --> 00:05:07.610
Nice timing on the reward...

00:05:09.240 --> 00:05:10.130
Sweet!

00:05:10.130 --> 00:05:10.900
Yum!

00:05:10.900 --> 00:05:12.580
It has a mild taste.

00:05:13.000 --> 00:05:17.600
If you keep stirring slowly 
and constantly over time...

00:05:19.790 --> 00:05:22.200
Oh? It's not so sweet anymore.

00:05:22.200 --> 00:05:24.110
It tastes more like tofu skin.

00:05:24.110 --> 00:05:25.260
I want soy sauce.

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:28.490
So all the lactose 
leached into the whey.

00:05:28.490 --> 00:05:29.720
Right.

00:05:30.970 --> 00:05:34.730
We discard a third of 
the lactose-rich whey

00:05:35.040 --> 00:05:37.340
and replace that amount 
with lukewarm water.

00:05:37.340 --> 00:05:39.190
That leaches even more 
of the lactose out.

00:05:39.550 --> 00:05:42.730
So we take advantage of osmotic 
pressure to remove the lactose.

00:05:43.210 --> 00:05:44.830
Neat.

00:05:44.830 --> 00:05:48.640
Cheese making is like chemistry! 
 It's fun!

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:52.030
Thinking of this like school 
stuff is making me sick.

00:05:52.270 --> 00:05:54.870
Place a lid and a weight 
on top to press the cheese.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:56.860
Now we can take a breather.

00:05:57.540 --> 00:05:59.330
I'm hungry...

00:05:59.330 --> 00:06:01.900
Come to think of it, 
we haven't had lunch yet.

00:06:02.530 --> 00:06:05.300
But there's still 
more work to be done,

00:06:05.300 --> 00:06:08.260
so we can't leave for too long.

00:06:08.600 --> 00:06:10.470
I'll go ask the dining hall lady

00:06:10.470 --> 00:06:13.190
to whip up something 
we can eat quickly!

00:06:13.190 --> 00:06:15.470
Ah, please do!

00:06:15.470 --> 00:06:17.090
Off I go!

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:20.520
Tokiwa-kun is quick on his feet.

00:06:20.520 --> 00:06:21.770
Though he's an idiot.

00:06:21.770 --> 00:06:24.210
He gets the job done.

00:06:24.210 --> 00:06:25.460
Though he's an idiot.

00:06:25.910 --> 00:06:27.550
I had them make lunch!

00:06:27.550 --> 00:06:29.610
Rice balls and natto rolls!

00:06:29.850 --> 00:06:31.280
Idiot!

00:06:31.660 --> 00:06:34.190
The bacteria in natto 
are very robust!

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:36.250
Don't bring that into the 
cheese processing room!

00:06:36.580 --> 00:06:41.560
So you can't eat natto for one day
 even before you make cheese.

00:06:41.560 --> 00:06:44.680
But natto rolls are so good.

00:06:45.610 --> 00:06:49.380
Man, it took an entire day 
just to prep the cheese.

00:06:49.380 --> 00:06:52.010
It's such a time-consuming food.

00:06:52.010 --> 00:06:54.250
Controlling the temperature 
isn't easy, either.

00:06:54.250 --> 00:06:58.460
Starter cultures and other additives 
have to be prepared in advance,

00:06:58.460 --> 00:07:01.230
so there's even more time 
going into it than you just saw.

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:04.290
Huh, wow.

00:07:07.130 --> 00:07:07.850
Welcome back!

00:07:07.850 --> 00:07:09.300
Is the cheese finished?

00:07:09.300 --> 00:07:11.990
It'll be ready in three months.

00:07:11.990 --> 00:07:13.600
It takes that long?

00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:16.200
And here I thought it'd 
be done right away.

00:07:16.200 --> 00:07:18.310
We have to wait till 
next year to eat it?

00:07:18.310 --> 00:07:21.000
It's not that easy to make.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:22.700
Yeah.

00:07:23.170 --> 00:07:25.140
But because of how that game went,

00:07:25.140 --> 00:07:28.170
I wanted to give some 
to Komaba to cheer him up.

00:07:30.550 --> 00:07:32.590
Yeah, that's true.

00:07:34.790 --> 00:07:37.430
I hope he'll come back soon.

00:07:37.880 --> 00:07:41.060
The group practicum takes that much 
longer when we're one man down.

00:07:42.370 --> 00:07:43.810
Yeah.

00:07:43.810 --> 00:07:46.770
<b>Komaba Ranch</b>

00:07:44.170 --> 00:07:46.770
That musclehead's 
going to get sluggish

00:07:47.090 --> 00:07:48.600
after taking such a long break.

00:07:51.670 --> 00:07:53.280
He's so big.

00:07:53.640 --> 00:07:54.660
Is he Fillet?

00:07:54.660 --> 00:07:56.200
That's Bacon!

00:07:56.610 --> 00:07:57.860
This is Cutlet,

00:07:57.860 --> 00:07:59.450
Ham, and Pork Soup.

00:07:59.450 --> 00:08:01.000
I'm surprised you 
can tell them apart.

00:08:01.000 --> 00:08:04.150
That's just how much I love them!

00:08:04.150 --> 00:08:05.950
Love doesn't fill an empty stomach.

00:08:05.950 --> 00:08:08.150
I wanna turn them into 
bacon and eat them soon.

00:08:08.150 --> 00:08:10.830
Bacon!

00:08:10.830 --> 00:08:12.130
Hey, Hachiken!

00:08:12.130 --> 00:08:13.260
About your help with calving—

00:08:13.260 --> 00:08:15.140
What, another birth?!

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:16.380
I'm not helping!

00:08:16.380 --> 00:08:18.290
No, not that.

00:08:18.290 --> 00:08:21.220
You helped out last time, right?

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:23.310
Want to name one of the calves?

00:08:25.140 --> 00:08:28.350
One's a female, so we're gonna 
keep her as a dairy cow.

00:08:28.350 --> 00:08:30.940
She's going to be placed
 permanently on the pedigree chart,

00:08:30.940 --> 00:08:32.320
so give her an official name.

00:08:32.600 --> 00:08:34.600
Me, a godfather?

00:08:34.600 --> 00:08:35.910
An official name?

00:08:36.310 --> 00:08:38.730
If she turns out to be a good one,
let's enter her in competitions.

00:08:38.730 --> 00:08:40.670
The Hol Club will gussy her up.

00:08:40.670 --> 00:08:42.980
I'll milk her, then.

00:08:44.130 --> 00:08:46.470
Oh, je t'aime!

00:08:45.300 --> 00:08:48.010
Nice bod, Miss!

00:08:48.010 --> 00:08:49.670
My daughter!

00:08:49.670 --> 00:08:51.080
Oh, je t'aime!

00:08:51.080 --> 00:08:52.890
You've got great boobies.

00:08:52.890 --> 00:08:54.380
My daughter!

00:08:54.380 --> 00:08:57.710
I think I understand 
how Mikage's dad feels.

00:08:57.710 --> 00:08:58.200
Huh?!

00:08:58.200 --> 00:08:59.640
Where'd that come from?!

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:04.020
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:09:04.020 --> 00:09:07.650
Let's make cheese again 
when she's ready to produce milk!

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:08.950
Good idea!

00:09:08.950 --> 00:09:11.780
Let me work on the whey-fed 
pork research, too.

00:09:12.120 --> 00:09:15.890
Y'know, I've had to do a lot of different things 
these past six months...

00:09:15.890 --> 00:09:20.500
But I think I've finally started to understand 
what makes agriculture enjoyable.

00:09:20.500 --> 00:09:24.210
Just like how cheese making 
is basically chemistry,

00:09:24.210 --> 00:09:27.040
you can focus on whatever 
plays to your strengths.

00:09:28.170 --> 00:09:30.090
Agriculture's deep, man!

00:09:30.090 --> 00:09:33.430
Don't talk like you've actually 
given it much thought.

00:09:33.430 --> 00:09:35.770
Well, to put it simply,

00:09:35.770 --> 00:09:38.410
agriculture is fun and tasty.

00:09:38.410 --> 00:09:39.530
That's true.

00:09:39.530 --> 00:09:42.220
You won't starve to death for sure.

00:09:42.220 --> 00:09:44.390
It's really a silver spoon.

00:09:44.390 --> 00:09:48.010
There's no risk of starving to death,
 even in this economy.

00:09:48.010 --> 00:09:50.860
Us farm kids really were born 
holding a silver spoon.

00:09:50.860 --> 00:09:53.640
My family's not that rich, though.

00:09:54.400 --> 00:09:56.060
Neither is mine!

00:09:57.310 --> 00:09:59.780
Oh, rich kid, right there.

00:10:02.950 --> 00:10:04.330
I've been kept waiting,

00:10:04.330 --> 00:10:06.510
Mikage Aki and Hachiken Whatever!

00:10:06.510 --> 00:10:09.360
You were so late that 
I helped myself to dinner!

00:10:09.360 --> 00:10:11.460
Don't put your feet up, you ingrate!

00:10:11.830 --> 00:10:14.330
What's wrong, Ayame-chan? 
Why are you here?

00:10:15.010 --> 00:10:16.420
I just came for a quick visit.

00:10:16.800 --> 00:10:19.440
I heard a spot's opening 
up in dairy science,

00:10:19.440 --> 00:10:20.720
so I thought I might transfer.

00:10:21.830 --> 00:10:22.510
Transfer?

00:10:22.750 --> 00:10:24.640
A spot's opening up?

00:10:25.720 --> 00:10:27.700
Oh...

00:10:27.700 --> 00:10:28.830
Me?!

00:10:28.830 --> 00:10:29.610
No, no, no.

00:10:29.610 --> 00:10:31.480
Wait, don't just assume 
I'm flunking out!

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:34.300
Transfer? You're switching schools.

00:10:34.300 --> 00:10:37.030
I thought that wasn't allowed unless 
there's a really good reason.

00:10:37.030 --> 00:10:39.270
Don't you have to retake 
the entrance exam?

00:10:39.270 --> 00:10:40.610
Huh?! Really?!

00:10:40.910 --> 00:10:43.300
Ayame-chan, how did you find out?

00:10:43.300 --> 00:10:44.760
How?

00:10:44.760 --> 00:10:47.690
My grandfather's the union president 
of the local agricultural co-op.

00:10:47.690 --> 00:10:50.330
We hear what's happening 
with all the local members.

00:10:51.080 --> 00:10:55.210
They got official notice for the 
Komaba Ranch yesterday, too.

00:10:57.660 --> 00:11:00.010
What's going on with 
Komaba's family?

00:11:00.010 --> 00:11:02.720
He didn't tell you anything?

00:11:02.720 --> 00:11:04.360
What's going on?!

00:11:07.350 --> 00:11:09.480
The Komaba Ranch is going to close.

00:11:09.910 --> 00:11:12.180
They can't pay their debts anymore.

00:11:12.180 --> 00:11:13.360
They're basically bankrupt.

00:11:15.780 --> 00:11:16.380
Huh?

00:11:18.140 --> 00:11:19.100
Bankrupt?

00:11:19.560 --> 00:11:23.120
Icchan's not coming back to school.

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:25.950
He's going to drop out.

00:11:26.290 --> 00:11:27.260
Huh?

00:11:27.260 --> 00:11:31.960
But, Komaba's gonna take over 
after he graduates, right?

00:11:31.960 --> 00:11:34.380
Or he was gonna go
 to nationals and turn pro...

00:11:34.730 --> 00:11:36.280
Right, Mikage?

00:11:38.170 --> 00:11:40.420
Wh-What? No warning...

00:11:41.040 --> 00:11:42.900
Wait, why didn't he tell us?!

00:11:42.900 --> 00:11:44.620
Mikage, you knew, right?

00:11:46.260 --> 00:11:47.960
She couldn't say anything, of course.

00:11:48.460 --> 00:11:51.780
The Komaba Ranch is a business
 and it's going bankrupt.

00:11:51.780 --> 00:11:53.280
You can't just go around 
spreading the news

00:11:53.280 --> 00:11:55.520
before the official notice goes out.

00:11:55.520 --> 00:11:58.610
Besides, could you have done anything, 
even if she told you?

00:11:58.880 --> 00:12:00.360
Can you pay off their debts?

00:12:01.840 --> 00:12:02.990
I'm sorry...

00:12:04.410 --> 00:12:07.660
Is there really nothing 
that can be done?! C'mon!

00:12:08.070 --> 00:12:09.550
Well...

00:12:09.550 --> 00:12:11.750
It is what it is.

00:12:11.750 --> 00:12:12.730
Yeah...

00:12:12.730 --> 00:12:14.550
It is what it is?

00:12:14.550 --> 00:12:16.330
That's so cold...

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:20.060
So Komaba really didn't 
tell you guys anything.

00:12:20.060 --> 00:12:23.120
In a way, that's just like him.

00:12:23.120 --> 00:12:24.570
That jerk...

00:12:24.570 --> 00:12:25.570
Damn!

00:12:25.570 --> 00:12:27.470
He doesn't have a cell!

00:12:27.800 --> 00:12:29.830
He doesn't have to quit school!

00:12:29.830 --> 00:12:32.360
He can still get better 
at baseball, too!

00:12:32.360 --> 00:12:35.900
He's going to get a job, so he can 
start repaying their debts right away.

00:12:36.210 --> 00:12:39.030
But... he said he'd 
go to nationals...

00:12:39.440 --> 00:12:41.820
Turn pro and get a bigger cattle shed...

00:12:42.540 --> 00:12:44.510
Make things easier for his mom...

00:12:45.830 --> 00:12:47.050
This can't be...

00:12:47.470 --> 00:12:50.610
Just like that? His dream's over?

00:12:55.030 --> 00:12:59.560
Icchan's dad passed away right 
after he expanded their business,

00:12:59.560 --> 00:13:01.510
so he left them deeply in debt.

00:13:02.020 --> 00:13:05.290
His mom tried to make 
things work by herself,

00:13:05.290 --> 00:13:06.220
but it didn't work out.

00:13:06.870 --> 00:13:10.600
His mom wanted Icchan 
to finish high school at least,

00:13:11.060 --> 00:13:14.140
but he insisted on quitting 
and starting work right away.

00:13:14.580 --> 00:13:17.820
Still, he did ask for one last chance.

00:13:18.360 --> 00:13:21.410
If he could keep winning in baseball 
and get a chance to turn pro,

00:13:21.410 --> 00:13:23.940
he could take care of the 
debt all at once, so...

00:13:24.460 --> 00:13:27.180
But he could make it 
to nationals next year!

00:13:27.180 --> 00:13:28.200
He can't give up now—

00:13:28.200 --> 00:13:32.540
No, their debt would just 
grow over time.

00:13:32.870 --> 00:13:35.090
Is it really too late?

00:13:35.090 --> 00:13:36.630
There's nothing we can do?

00:13:36.630 --> 00:13:39.400
Hachiken-kun, you're really a nice guy.

00:13:40.290 --> 00:13:42.550
But you really can't 
do anything about this.

00:13:43.470 --> 00:13:46.260
Don't get too down about it.

00:13:46.610 --> 00:13:49.580
Remember how you're supposed 
to let go right away

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:52.220
when you fall off a horse 
and hit the ground?

00:13:52.660 --> 00:13:56.960
If you don't let go, you'll get 
dragged by the horse and get hurt.

00:13:56.960 --> 00:13:59.560
You don't need to hurt 
yourself for no reason.

00:13:59.560 --> 00:14:00.910
But...

00:14:00.910 --> 00:14:01.600
Still!

00:14:01.600 --> 00:14:03.260
Let go of the reins.

00:14:04.080 --> 00:14:07.930
I don't want you to suffer.

00:14:09.020 --> 00:14:10.790
I'm going back to my room.

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:12.950
Mikage!

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:24.240
If you keep looking down,

00:14:24.240 --> 00:14:27.260
you're just asking 
for bad luck to linger.

00:14:28.040 --> 00:14:33.010
I've never liked how you keep 
your emotions bottled up inside,

00:14:33.010 --> 00:14:38.010
but I'm not sure I like watching 
you without the fake smile, either.

00:14:42.440 --> 00:14:46.940
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:45.900
Is there nothing I can do?

00:14:46.940 --> 00:14:49.150
<b>Campus Motto
Defy Logic  Cooperation  Diligence</b>

00:14:49.540 --> 00:14:52.020
We have debt, too,
 so it hits close to home.

00:14:52.020 --> 00:14:54.370
Can your pops repay 
it in his lifetime?

00:14:54.370 --> 00:14:57.610
My family said we'll get more cows 
once I take over the business.

00:14:57.610 --> 00:14:59.750
How much does it cost to 
renovate a cattle shed?

00:14:59.750 --> 00:15:02.630
People are drinking less milk nowadays, right?

00:15:02.630 --> 00:15:04.380
So you want to process 
the milk to add value?

00:15:04.380 --> 00:15:06.680
Maybe it'll be all about cheese now.

00:15:06.680 --> 00:15:08.670
You're not considering 
joint management?

00:15:08.940 --> 00:15:13.430
I guess this is what he meant when 
he said he has no time for girls.

00:15:14.880 --> 00:15:18.820
Everyone's more worried about their 
own businesses than about Komaba.

00:15:18.820 --> 00:15:21.140
No, they're worried about him!

00:15:21.440 --> 00:15:24.500
But there's nothing you can do. 
 That's just the reality of it.

00:15:24.500 --> 00:15:28.120
You don't know if it'll be you next.

00:15:28.750 --> 00:15:31.320
Is Komaba really dropping out?

00:15:31.740 --> 00:15:34.250
His stuff's still in his room,

00:15:34.250 --> 00:15:36.800
so he might still come back.

00:15:37.440 --> 00:15:40.790
In any case, I'd like to 
hear his side of the story.

00:15:41.500 --> 00:15:42.810
I feel sick...

00:15:42.810 --> 00:15:44.020
You okay?

00:15:44.020 --> 00:15:44.890
No...

00:15:44.890 --> 00:15:46.540
I'll go ask to be excused 
from classes today.

00:15:46.540 --> 00:15:50.490
Maybe he's still worn out 
from the festival.

00:15:50.490 --> 00:15:52.510
Don't collapse again!

00:15:52.510 --> 00:15:54.470
<b>Ooezo Agricultural High School Dormitory for Future Agriculture Managers</b>

00:15:54.470 --> 00:15:55.930
A Aoyama Rei 

00:15:56.320 --> 00:15:58.010
<b>Math I</b>

00:16:00.980 --> 00:16:02.440
I knew it.

00:16:02.440 --> 00:16:03.630
Whoa!

00:16:03.630 --> 00:16:04.870
What, Hachiken?

00:16:04.870 --> 00:16:05.730
What about classes?

00:16:05.730 --> 00:16:07.470
I played sick.

00:16:07.470 --> 00:16:08.980
You played sick?

00:16:08.980 --> 00:16:13.560
No one doubts me since
 I'm always so responsible.

00:16:14.150 --> 00:16:15.740
Given the kind of guy you are,

00:16:15.740 --> 00:16:19.630
I thought you'd sneak in to get your things
 when no one was around.

00:16:19.630 --> 00:16:23.020
I was waiting for you, 
and hit the jackpot!

00:16:24.140 --> 00:16:25.710
You sneak...

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:26.790
<b>Livestock Science 
  -Hokkaido-</b>

00:16:28.130 --> 00:16:29.690
You're really dropping out?

00:16:29.690 --> 00:16:30.630
Yeah.

00:16:30.630 --> 00:16:34.050
I already said my farewells 
to the teachers and the field manager.

00:16:35.130 --> 00:16:36.800
Why are you doing it?

00:16:37.180 --> 00:16:38.800
I heard you already know.

00:16:38.800 --> 00:16:41.260
We're shutting down because of our debt.

00:16:41.260 --> 00:16:42.770
I'm gonna quit school and start working.

00:16:42.770 --> 00:16:46.460
But your mom said you should 
finish high school, right?

00:16:46.460 --> 00:16:49.610
Why do you insist on 
quitting and working?

00:16:52.070 --> 00:16:54.310
If I don't work and earn money,

00:16:54.310 --> 00:16:56.640
I'm going to be a 
burden to Aki's family.

00:16:56.640 --> 00:16:58.830
I mean, I already am.

00:16:58.830 --> 00:17:00.630
Mikage's family?

00:17:00.630 --> 00:17:01.570
Why?

00:17:05.170 --> 00:17:08.250
When Dad needed a loan 
to expand the business,

00:17:08.250 --> 00:17:10.250
they agreed to co-sign.

00:17:13.010 --> 00:17:16.180
So this will affect 
their business, too.

00:17:16.180 --> 00:17:20.070
That's why I have to hurry to 
repay the loan as soon as possible.

00:17:21.640 --> 00:17:25.040
Our farm land's way in the boonies,

00:17:25.570 --> 00:17:27.870
so it'd only sell for 
pennies even if we tried.

00:17:29.300 --> 00:17:32.940
Most of our cows are old, 
so we'd get swindled there, too.

00:17:33.430 --> 00:17:35.530
I want to let my little 
sisters go to college,

00:17:36.020 --> 00:17:37.530
so I'm gonna quit school and work.

00:17:37.800 --> 00:17:39.580
But, what about your dreams?!

00:17:39.580 --> 00:17:41.080
Are you gonna give up?!

00:17:41.080 --> 00:17:42.790
You were working so hard!

00:17:43.540 --> 00:17:44.870
Yeah...

00:17:45.330 --> 00:17:49.510
I've lost them all. Baseball, 
taking over the business, everything.

00:17:51.190 --> 00:17:52.340
It can't be helped.

00:17:55.050 --> 00:17:56.670
Thank you for your help.

00:17:56.960 --> 00:17:58.530
I've cleared out.

00:17:58.530 --> 00:17:59.670
Hello.

00:17:59.670 --> 00:18:01.140
Oh, Hachiken-kun!

00:18:01.140 --> 00:18:02.570
It's been a while!

00:18:03.000 --> 00:18:04.540
What about your classes?

00:18:04.540 --> 00:18:06.690
Sensei, he faked it.

00:18:06.690 --> 00:18:08.100
I knew it.

00:18:10.560 --> 00:18:13.160
Thank you for the bacon, by the way!

00:18:13.160 --> 00:18:14.700
It was delicious!

00:18:14.700 --> 00:18:16.900
Th-Thank you.

00:18:17.930 --> 00:18:20.990
Hachiken-kun, stay in school.

00:18:23.570 --> 00:18:24.740
Take care.

00:18:25.090 --> 00:18:27.240
Stop by sometimes.

00:18:28.130 --> 00:18:29.510
Thank you for taking care of me.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:36.120
Don't look like that.

00:18:36.120 --> 00:18:37.270
You're gonna collapse

00:18:37.270 --> 00:18:39.880
from other people's problems 
if you don't stop it.

00:18:41.270 --> 00:18:43.580
It's not unusual for farms to shut down.

00:18:43.580 --> 00:18:46.480
I've already come to terms with it.

00:18:46.480 --> 00:18:48.640
So don't go on and on about 
other people's problems.

00:18:54.600 --> 00:18:56.550
Shut up, jerk!

00:18:57.150 --> 00:19:00.400
So you're all calm and collected 
because you know how it is, huh?

00:19:00.400 --> 00:19:03.450
You're just gonna brace 
yourself and face it, all zen?

00:19:03.860 --> 00:19:05.290
Every single one of you...

00:19:05.620 --> 00:19:08.330
all going, "That's how it is," 
"There's nothing you can do..."

00:19:09.870 --> 00:19:12.400
But I know you're 
boiling over inside!

00:19:12.400 --> 00:19:14.770
Don't try to make it sound 
like it's no big deal!

00:19:14.770 --> 00:19:18.630
I hate what you're telling me!

00:19:33.190 --> 00:19:34.210
Hey...

00:19:34.210 --> 00:19:36.900
Hachiken-kun, are you feeling better?

00:19:37.220 --> 00:19:38.120
Yeah.

00:19:38.840 --> 00:19:42.660
Komaba cleaned out his room today.

00:19:43.490 --> 00:19:44.710
I see.

00:19:48.560 --> 00:19:52.920
I heard from Komaba that 
your family co-signed his loan.

00:19:54.070 --> 00:19:56.510
He said that's why he's 
going straight to work,

00:19:56.510 --> 00:19:58.300
to avoid being a burden to you guys.

00:19:59.090 --> 00:20:02.420
I told him not to worry about us,

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:03.840
but Icchan's so stubborn.

00:20:04.540 --> 00:20:07.270
I'm glad you found out everything.

00:20:08.390 --> 00:20:09.770
So, yeah. That's the deal.

00:20:10.290 --> 00:20:13.740
Let's not dwell on it, okay?

00:20:13.740 --> 00:20:14.810
Let's forget about it!

00:20:14.810 --> 00:20:15.690
Mika—

00:20:15.690 --> 00:20:17.090
It's got nothing to do with you.

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:18.940
Nothing that involves 
you, Hachiken-kun.

00:20:20.890 --> 00:20:22.280
<i>Yeah...</i>

00:20:23.020 --> 00:20:24.610
<i>What am I thinking?</i>

00:20:24.610 --> 00:20:26.720
<i>Bankruptcy? Co-signing loans?</i>

00:20:26.720 --> 00:20:28.690
<i>I'm a total outsider.</i>

00:20:29.160 --> 00:20:30.700
<i>Even if I make a fuss,</i>

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:33.540
<i>won't I just stir things 
up for Komaba and Mikage</i>

00:20:33.540 --> 00:20:35.960
<i>after they've finally come 
to terms with everything?</i>

00:20:37.710 --> 00:20:39.460
Some students struggle to 
talk about how they feel,

00:20:39.460 --> 00:20:41.390
even though they're suffering.

00:20:41.390 --> 00:20:42.730
<i>That's right.</i>

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:44.800
<i>They can't be okay with all this!</i>

00:20:44.800 --> 00:20:46.430
<i>Just think about how they looked.</i>

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:49.240
You need to ask for 
help when you need it.

00:20:49.240 --> 00:20:50.890
<i>He's the one who needed it!</i>

00:20:50.890 --> 00:20:52.850
Let go of the reins.

00:20:53.180 --> 00:20:57.190
I don't want you to suffer.

00:20:57.720 --> 00:20:59.400
<i>Every single one of them...</i>

00:21:00.420 --> 00:21:02.810
<i>Even though they're 
the ones suffering...</i>

00:21:04.660 --> 00:21:06.080
Idiots!

00:21:06.820 --> 00:21:09.660
Don't worry about me!

00:21:10.290 --> 00:21:12.580
How could I forget about 
you guys, you idiots?!

00:21:12.580 --> 00:21:14.080
Drag me into it!

00:21:14.080 --> 00:21:15.750
Kick me in the head! The stomach!

00:21:15.750 --> 00:21:17.130
It's all fine by me!

00:22:45.690 --> 00:22:50.260
This story is a work of fiction.
